From 5be0794730e9f33ec92100380833c9b5b792fbb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:09:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] USB: format as ext4 / ext3 / ext2; fix NTFS and HFS+
 formatting from the Reaper USB page

e2fsprogs' mke2fs already ships in the image (its default profile is
compiled in, so -t ext4 needs no /etc/mke2fs.conf) and the mount path has
handled ext2/3/4 all along - only the format dispatch in rc/usb.c lacked
the cases. Added: mke2fs -F -t <ext2|ext3|ext4> -m 1 -L <label>, whole
device, same shape as the Tuxera tools. The mkfs.ext4 link is no longer
gated on RTCONFIG_EXT4FS (hard-set n), matching the earlier fsck.ext4 fix.

Field defect found on the way: Reaper_USB.asp posted "ntfs"/"hfs" where
rc/usb.c only accepts the Tuxera names "tntfs"/"thfsplus" (the stock
device-map/disk_format.asp uses those), so NTFS and HFS+ formatting from
the Reaper page silently did nothing - the log said "w/o tool" and the disk
was re-mounted untouched. Values corrected.

Page: the selector lists FAT32, ext4, ext3, ext2 (+ NTFS / HFS+ when the
Tuxera modules are present) with a one-line hint per choice (RDST_65-67,
English in all 25 dicts).
